# FRONTEND ENGINEERING STANDARD
Build reusable, maintainable interfaces.
## BEFORE ADDING CODE
Search the codebase for:
- existing components
- existing tokens
- existing utility classes
- existing responsive patterns
- existing animations
- existing typography
- existing image components
Reuse before creating.
## DESIGN TOKENS
Prefer centralized tokens for:
- colors
- spacing
- typography
- radii
- shadows
- transitions
- breakpoints
Do not scatter arbitrary values throughout components.
If repeated values appear, consider promoting them into the design system.
## COMPONENTS
Create components around meaningful UI patterns.
Do not over-abstract tiny elements.
Do not duplicate substantial UI.
## CSS
Prefer:
- predictable layout systems
- CSS variables/tokens
- grid/flex
- responsive constraints
- fluid sizing where appropriate
- component-level consistency
Avoid:
- arbitrary magic numbers
- excessive absolute positioning
- unnecessary z-index layers
- viewport-specific hacks
- duplicated media queries
## RESPONSIVE
Test meaningful breakpoints.
Pay special attention to:
- navigation
- typography
- card grids
- hero sections
- imagery
- horizontal overflow
- button sizing
- section spacing
## PERFORMANCE
Do not add expensive effects without reason.
Optimize large images.
Avoid unnecessary client-side rendering.
Do not introduce libraries just to solve a small styling problem.
## ACCESSIBILITY
Use semantic HTML.
Maintain keyboard navigation.
Maintain focus visibility.
Use appropriate labels.
Respect reduced motion.
## FINAL CHECK
After implementation:
- check console errors
- check layout
- check responsiveness
- check interaction
- inspect the actual rendered UI
